{"id":"ahitub","name":"Ahitub","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ahitub"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ahitub","text":"Brother of goodness = good. (1.) The son of Phinehas. On the death of his grandfather Eli he succeeded to the office of high priest, and was himself succeeded by his son Ahijah (1 Sam. 14:3; 22:9, 11, 12, 20). (2.) The father of Zadok, who was made high priest by Saul after the extermination of the family of Ahimelech (1 Chr. 6:7, 8; 2 Sam. 8:17)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H285","lemma":"אֲחִיטוּב","xlit":"ʼĂchîyṭûwb","gloss":"Achitub, the name of several priests","kjv":"Ahitub","count":12,"share":0.92},{"strong":"H6659","lemma":"צָדוֹק","xlit":"Tsâdôwq","gloss":"Tsadok, the name of eight or nine Israelites","kjv":"Zadok","count":7,"share":0.54},{"strong":"H288","lemma":"אֲחִימֶלֶךְ","xlit":"ʼĂchîymelek","gloss":"Achimelek, the name of an Israelite and of a Hittite","kjv":"Ahimelech","count":4,"share":0.31},{"strong":"H54","lemma":"אֶבְיָתָר","xlit":"ʼEbyâthâr","gloss":"Ebjathar, an Israelite","kjv":"Abiathar","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H5838","lemma":"עֲזַרְיָה","xlit":"ʻĂzaryâh","gloss":"Azarjah, the name of nineteen Israelites","kjv":"Azariah","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H5011","lemma":"נֹב","xlit":"Nôb","gloss":"Nob, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Nob","count":2,"share":0.15}],"verses":["1Sam.14.3","1Sam.22.9","1Sam.22.11","1Sam.22.12","1Sam.22.20","2Sam.8.17","1Chr.6.8","1Chr.6.11","1Chr.6.12","1Chr.9.11","1Chr.18.16","Neh.11.11","2Chr.31.10"],"related":[{"id":"ahimelech","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.154,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"abiathar","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.118,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"shallum","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.086,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"azariah","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.082,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"seraiah","type":"cooccur","sh